No macOS tooling, and no skills that are useless here
====================================================

Two halves of the same complaint: the Tools & skills page listed things that cannot work on this
machine and things that nobody on Linux wants.

  * the `applescript` MCP server is no longer seeded, and the loop that re-added anything missing no
    longer pushes it back — it was removed by hand and returned on the next launch. Gated on
    `cfg!(target_os = "macos")`, because on Linux every call to it fails, which reads as a broken
    feature rather than an absent one
  * the bundled skill set is pruned to `browser-driving`. Dropped: docx, pdf, pdf-reading, pptx, xlsx,
    frontend-design — office-document skills for a Linux desktop, where the answer is a shell and an
    editor. They can be re-added per machine; they should not be the default face of the page

Nothing is deleted from the codebase: `applescript_tools()` still exists for the macOS build, and the
skills remain in the upstream repository the bundle was cut from.

